WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
You step off a long overnight flight.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.540
Where you've landed, it's breakfast time.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.970
But the clock inside you
says it's 3 in the morning.

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.130
You yawn.

5
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.250
Your eyes feel heavy.

6
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.780
Two clocks, hours apart.

7
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.860
So what brings them back together?

8
00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.460
What resets the clock inside you?

9
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.360
In this mission, you'll discover
that your body runs its own rhythm,

10
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.690
repeating about every 24
hours: the circadian rhythm.

11
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.270
You'll meet the pineal
gland, and melatonin,

12
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.320
the hormone that makes you sleepy.

13
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.930
And you'll find out about
zeitgebers, or time-givers:

14
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.070
cues from outside your body.

15
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.090
But which one matters most?

16
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: work out what resets
your body clock after a long flight.
